WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
The day it was January 9th, 2023,

00:00:01.964 --> 00:00:06.760
[music] and I posted my very first

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.680
YouTube video. And I frankly had a lot

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.080
of maybe unrealistic expectations. I

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.200
thought YouTube was going to make me

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.240
tons and tons of money, maybe open some

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.480
new doors for me. I really thought I was

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.680
going to blow up overnight. What I

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.880
didn't understand back then is that

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.480
YouTube does not reward virality or

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.720
hustle at first. It rewards skills,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:28.400
systems, and relationships. And once I

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.560
understood that, everything changed. But

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.240
how do you actually achieve growth and

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.840
more importantly monetization with

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.000
things like systems and relationships?

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.990
Well, that's what this video is all

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.400
about. So, let's dive in.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.920
>> [music]

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.320
>> Your biggest mistake on YouTube is not

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.160
that you're doing it wrong. It's that

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.880
you might be expecting results way too

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.840
early. When I first started my YouTube

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.560
channel, I thought effort obviously

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.400
equals results. If I showed up

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.400
consistently, learned the rules, and

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.240
followed advice, I thought honestly the

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.400
algorithm would reward me fairly

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.240
quickly. In fact, on my second month on

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.360
YouTube, I actually decided to challenge

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.280
myself to posting a long-form video

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.199
every single day. I was like, "Surely

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.680
this will get a video to go viral." But

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.960
what I didn't realize is that YouTube

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.280
really does not work on a linear

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.720
timeline. In the beginning when you

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.200
start a YouTube channel, your effort is

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.920
mostly going to turn into skills rather

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.760
than views. And honestly, that's

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.520
frustrating because your skills are

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.680
invisible. But it is so, so crucial. No

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.240
one is there to see that you're spending

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.120
hours filming, editing, re-editing,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.080
re-filming, [music]

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.840
or like most people doubting yourself.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.960
But the truth is that these repetitions

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.640
are absolutely necessary to have a

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.400
successful channel. Think of it this

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.120
way. You wouldn't go to the gym for the

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.680
first time in your entire life and show

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.200
up and expect to be the strongest person

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.120
there able to lift more weights than

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.000
anybody else at the gym, right? No. You

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.480
would show up day after day. You would

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.920
learn the best ways to achieve your

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.080
goals, and you would put in the

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.120
practice. Over time, you start to see

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.000
those results that you're working

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.880
towards, whether that be being stronger

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.280
or having bigger muscles or whatever.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.040
But here's the dangerous part with

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.760
YouTube. When YouTube doesn't give you

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.920
results early, your brain is going to

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.640
start thinking that you're doing

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.280
something wrong. So, maybe you change

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.880
your direction too fast, you lose

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.640
confidence, or you stop trusting

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.479
yourself. And that is usually the

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.680
beginning of the end. So, most people

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:09.520
actually end up quitting here because

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.760
they confuse no traction with no

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.240
progress. But progress is happening,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.040
just maybe not in the way that you

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.480
expected it to. So, just know that if

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.400
you're early and feeling a little bit

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.800
frustrated, it does not mean that you

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.720
are failing. It just means that you're

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.720
still in that training phase, that

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.280
building up your reps phase. And that

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.120
panic of feeling like I wasn't growing

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.959
fast enough is what sent me into a

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.360
YouTube research rabbit hole. And that's

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:32.880
actually where things got even messier

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.840
for me, because I started watching

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.959
various different YouTube videos, tip

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.640
after tip of different ways to grow your

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:40.520
channel, how to have more watch hours,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.480
how to have more interesting titles or

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:44.720
thumbnails. And what that did was

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.080
actually make me spiral even more. So

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.640
then, how do you actually know what

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.320
advice to take when it comes to growing

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.480
a YouTube channel? The truth is that

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.000
most of those videos actually do have

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.640
valuable information. Most of that

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.080
advice does work, but you have to

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.000
understand that not all of it is going

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.640
to be perfect for you. The reality is,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.880
if you go to that YouTube search bar and

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.360
type in how to grow on YouTube, every

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.000
video is going to tell you something a

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.400
little bit different. Post long form,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.640
no, post shorts. Niche down, actually be

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.920
broad. Be high energy, be calm. Follow

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.519
trends, ignore them.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.360
Instead of helping, this actually then

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:15.519
ends up creating analysis paralysis

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.120
where you're just not sure which

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:18.560
direction to go. And that's actually

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.480
partially what led me to doing that

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.480
little mini challenge back in February

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.239
of 2023, because I decided that I

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.880
actually wanted to test out different

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:28.200
types of videos to figure out what I

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.160
liked making the best, what would work

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.239
best for me. When I posted every single

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.480
day, the biggest benefit was not

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:35.920
actually growth, it was clarity. I

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.959
finally started seeing patterns in my

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.560
content, things that people, my viewers,

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:41.360
were more interested in, and things that

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.480
I was more passionate talking about.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.080
Now, I just want to say here, you do not

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.200
need to go out and do a whole 30-day

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.160
challenge, because trust me, that was a

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.239
lot of work. What I am trying to say is

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.880
take the bits and pieces of advice from

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:54.800
other YouTubers that resonate the

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.680
strongest with you. YouTube is kind of

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.280
like learning how to cook, for example.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.480
Everyone can follow, you know, the same

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.000
recipe, but at the end of the day, each

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.400
one of us are going to have slightly

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.120
different skill sets, things that we

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.880
enjoy cooking more. You don't need to

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.200
follow a perfect recipe, you have to

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.440
find the perfect recipe for you. And by

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.200
the way, if you're in that phase where

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.959
you want to experiment, but maybe you

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.920
just don't know what to post, I actually

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:19.359
have a completely free list of over 100

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.320
YouTube video ideas that span across 10

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:22.880
different YouTube niches. I really made

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.640
this to help you get out of that spiral

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.400
and just start creating. So, if you're

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.240
curious about that list, I will link it

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.040
down in my description box. So, if you

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.680
feel like you've been watching other

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.400
people's videos, learning,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.640
experimenting, and still not making

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:37.000
progress, then fear not because this

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.040
next bit of information is going to be

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.240
super helpful. The good news is that

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.240
every video you post is quietly making

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.520
the next one a little bit easier. As

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.600
long as you focus on the right things.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.760
When I look back on my earlier videos,

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.320
everything felt a little bit hard. I

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.600
felt like talking to the camera was

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.800
really awkward. I honestly didn't even

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.120
really want to build scripts because

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.040
that felt like too much for me. Editing

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.280
took forever. I would overanalyze my

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.200
thumbnails. And the mistake I was making

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:06.360
was trying to fix and do everything at

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.040
once. This was my first real lesson in

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.640
building skills instead of chasing

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.919
growth. What actually improved my

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.560
channel was focusing on one skill at a

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:15.040
time. For certain videos, I didn't worry

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:17.360
about fancy editing, I just really

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.400
focused on my camera presence. Then,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.360
after that, I shifted to focusing on

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.680
thumbnails that were a little bit more

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.000
contrasty. And then, most recently, I

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.120
focused on tightening up my scripts so

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.560
that my videos have clear, concise

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.400
storylines and pathways rather than

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.000
feeling a little bit jumbled. So, here's

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.160
something practical that you can do if

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.160
you really want to hone in your skills.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.200
Pick one skill that you can improve for

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.040
your next 10 videos. Don't try to fix

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.200
everything, just pick one thing that you

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.320
can improve. Maybe it's your hook. Focus

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.480
on making the best hook that you can for

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.400
your next 10 videos. Maybe it's your

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:52.120
pacing, maybe you're rambling too much,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.760
maybe it's your audio quality. Let

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:56.280
everything else be good enough while you

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.080
focus on mastering this one skill and

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.120
then move on to the next one. And this

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.800
is how skill stacking actually works.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:03.200
Each layer is going to make the next one

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:05.280
easier because you're already going to

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:07.480
be a master at the last one. And then

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.440
over time, I'm talking months of time,

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:11.160
once those stacked skills start working

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.920
together, YouTube stops feeling like

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.880
constant effort and starts feeling like

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.120
momentum. And speaking of momentum, how

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.960
do you actually get that momentum

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:20.040
flowing? So, let's talk about the

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.280
momentum flywheel. Imagine trying to

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:24.000
push a massive flywheel. At first,

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.520
nothing is budging, no matter how hard

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.480
you try. That is early YouTube days,

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:31.280
tons of effort, almost no visible

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:33.200
motion. But every push matters. Slowly,

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.880
momentum builds and eventually the wheel

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.320
starts moving on its own. One video

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.200
leads to another, ideas start

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.200
connecting, opportunities start showing

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:42.080
up, etc. So, how do you actually get

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.320
this momentum flywheel going? And more

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.120
importantly, how do you actually make it

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.520
feel effortless so that you're not

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.280
constantly feeling like you're putting

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.240
in a ton of effort. So, what actually

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:52.400
has helped me build my momentum is not

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:54.440
posting more, it's working more

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.200
effectively. So, I actually built an

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.880
actual workflow that I'm following for

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.160
my YouTube channel. Now, remember, this

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.720
is not something that I did at the

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.080
beginning. I just started this like

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.600
three or four months ago. Of course, if

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.120
you start this at the beginning of your

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:07.000
YouTube channel, it might make your life

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.840
a lot easier, a lot faster. Learn from

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.840
my mistakes. So, here's how my workflow

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:13.280
kind of looks. I now spend a few days,

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:15.600
up to a week, just doing researching and

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.480
ideation. I just ideate dump video

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.760
ideas. Then from there, I actually

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:21.040
schedule them out over the span of like

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:23.000
two to three months depending on how

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.640
many strong video ideas I have. Then I

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.520
move into a scripting phase. I try to

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:28.600
script at least three videos [music] at

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.280
a time because typically when I sit down

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.160
and film in the next phase, I will try

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.640
and film three videos at a time. This

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.880
really helps me actually save time in

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.200
the long run because when I'm doing

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.160
things like ideating, I can just kind of

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.480
get in a flow of thinking of new ideas.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.120
[music] Same thing for scripting, I can

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:44.080
get into kind of a scripting flow. And

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.640
especially for filming because I am a

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.160
stay-at-home mom and I'm filming while

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.040
my daughter naps. She's napping right

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.560
now. I only have to set up my YouTube

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.160
setup once and film once. So, this is

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:55.120
where systems start to really do the

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.720
work for you instead of momentum. If you

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.040
want to give this a try, I recommend

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.400
spend a few days working on ideation,

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:02.480
maybe just two to three days on

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.400
scripting, pick one day to film a

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.160
handful of videos, then you have, you

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.640
know, two, three, or four videos that

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.320
you can just focus on editing for a

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.000
little bit. Remember that momentum is

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.880
not actually about energy, it's about

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.240
systems. The hardest part of starting a

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.400
YouTube channel is the beginning and

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.960
it's not because you're bad, it's

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.400
because the momentum has not started

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.919
building yet, that confidence has not

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.760
started building, your workflow has not

00:08:19.919 --> 00:08:23.919
started building. So, give that little

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.520
workflow a try and let me know if it

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:27.280
helps you reduce some friction and save

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.480
you time in the long run. And lastly, I

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.320
wanted to share the key that I wish I

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.719
knew way sooner, which is that

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.840
subscriber count does not matter. In

00:08:33.719 --> 00:08:36.280
fact, that's not how you're actually

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.760
going to grow and have a successful

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.159
YouTube channel. For a long time,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.320
especially at the beginning, I was

00:08:39.159 --> 00:08:43.440
really measuring my YouTube channel in

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:45.640
numbers. And I was so focused on having

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.880
a video go viral. And then, guess what?

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:50.080
I actually did have a video go viral.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.080
And unfortunately, that taught me that

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.920
virality is not all that it's cracked up

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.839
to be. I sort of wish that, you know,

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.760
that video hadn't popped off. The reason

00:08:55.839 --> 00:09:00.280
for that is because that video gained me

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:03.200
thousands and thousands of subscribers

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:04.966
that only cared about that one topic.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:06.839
So, a lot of times when I post videos

00:09:04.966 --> 00:09:09.080
[music] slightly outside of that niche,

00:09:06.839 --> 00:09:11.280
they tend to not perform as well.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:13.240
YouTube works the best when you actually

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.080
stop thinking about subscribers and

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:17.600
